<td><font face="verdana" size="3"><b>New levels of Slaying&#33;</b></font></td>
<td><div align="right"><font class="body">Posted on Jan. 29 2002,20:00 by <A HREF="http://207.199.33.115/cgi-bin/ikonboard.cgi?act=Profile&CODE=03&MID=103-1008803061">granyte</A></font></td></div>
</tr>
</table>
<table cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0" bgcolor="#000000" width="90%" align="center">
<tr>
<table cellspacing="4" cellpadding="0" bgcolor="#EEEEEE" width="100%" align="center">
<td><hr noshade size="1" color="#000000"><font face="verdana" size="2">A couple days back Ancient Council has probably one of it&#39;s crowning achievements when about 40 of us went to Temple of Veeshan and attempted our first West Wings ToV dragon, Gozzrem. &nbsp;It took us 2 failed attempts, however 3rd times a charm and we took him down at last. &nbsp;Our first attempt went well at first, however due to a problem with transitioning between main tanks we only got him to the 2nd Z on Gozzrem, so we knew that if things went smoothly we could beat him. &nbsp;Our second attempt started off bad quickly when we had a Complete Healing wurm add into the fray, not what we needed so we just camped out as many as possible to try again. &nbsp;Finally things came together, it was late at night and we had lost a few people, however most were able to stay and Gozzrem was finally put down. YAY. &nbsp;To date this is by far our biggest achievement, however we plan on growing from there ASAP <!--emo&:)--><img src="http://207.199.33.115/iB_html/non-cgi/emoticons/smile.gif" border="0" valign="absmiddle" alt=':)'><!--endemo-->.<br><br>HUGE grats to Vendric on the Eye of Rigtorgn, and to Nannoc on the Circlet of Silver Eyes, and Sadr on the Wand of the Black Dragon Eye. &nbsp;Grats to someone else on the dragon meat LOL <!--emo&:)--><img src="http://207.199.33.115/iB_html/non-cgi/emoticons/smile.gif" border="0" valign="absmiddle" alt=':)'><!--endemo--><br><br><br><img src="http://pages.sprint.ca/granyte/files/pics/Gozzrem_Dead.jpg" border="0"><p></font></td>
</tr>
</table>
</td>
</tr>
</table>
