<td><font face="verdana" size="3"><b>Wizard Epic, grats Rattiusmaximus</b></font></td>
<td><div align="right"><font class="body">Posted on Jan. 14 2002,18:29 by <A HREF="http://207.199.33.115/cgi-bin/ikonboard.cgi?act=Profile&CODE=03&MID=103-1008803061">granyte</A></font></td></div>
</tr>
</table>
<table cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0" bgcolor="#000000" width="90%" align="center">
<tr>
<table cellspacing="4" cellpadding="0" bgcolor="#EEEEEE" width="100%" align="center">
<td><hr noshade size="1" color="#000000"><font face="verdana" size="2">Needless to say, this is probably one of the most annoying epic quests out there. &nbsp;Day in, day out, Rattiusmaximus took his adventurers into the depths of Kedge keep, laying waste to Phinigel Autotrops again and again. &nbsp;Finally, after a dozen plus kills, Phinigel had dropped the blue crystal staff needed for Rattius to complete his epic. &nbsp;Grats on a job well done &#33;&#33;<br><br><img src="http://pages.sprint.ca/granyte/files/pics/rattepic.jpg" border="0"><p></font></td>
</tr>
</table>
